    "result_text": "The acceptance suite is the whole test suite (58 tests, all green). The change is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented owner deletion as a soft-delete. The changes:\n\n**Domain model** \u2014 `Owner.java`\n- Added a `deleted` boolean field (`@Column(name = \"deleted\")`, primitive so it defaults to `false`) with `isDeleted()`/`setDeleted(...)` accessors.\n\n**API contract** \u2014 `openapi.yml`\n- Added a read-only `deleted` boolean property to the `Owner` schema (and to its `required` list) so the generated `OwnerDto` carries it and MapStruct maps it automatically in both directions.\n\n**Database schema** \u2014 `db/{hsqldb,h2,mysql,postgres}/schema.sql`\n- Added a `deleted BOOLEAN DEFAULT FALSE NOT NULL` column (`BIT(1) DEFAULT 0` for MySQL) so retained rows and seed data are non-deleted by default.\n\n**Controller** \u2014 `OwnerRestControllerV1.java`\n- `deleteOwner`: instead of removing the record, it now sets `deleted = true` and saves the owner, still returning `204 No Content` (2xx). The row is retained.\n- `addOwner`: the household-duplicate and identity-key checks now filter out owners flagged `deleted`, so a normally-blocking duplicate is allowed when the only matching owner has been soft-deleted.\n\n**Behavior verified against the spec:**\n- A newly created owner has `deleted` = false.\n- `DELETE /api/owners/{id}` marks the owner deleted, retains the row, returns 2xx.\n- `GET /api/owners/{id}` still returns the owner afterward with `deleted` = true.\n- Re-creating an owner whose only match was soft-deleted now succeeds.\n\nTest results: `Tests run: 58, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 **BUILD SUCCESS**, including the new `Cp46Tests` (soft-delete flag/retain, and deleted-owner ignored by the duplicate check).",
